| Repeat Build (no-op) | 0.034s (min: 0.033s, max: 0.036s) | 0.205s (min: 0.204s, max: 0.207s) | +503.9% |
| Incremental Build (app) | 0.157s (min: 0.156s, max: 0.168s) | 0.339s (min: 0.325s, max: 0.358s) | +115.3% |

* Instrumented builds use the explicit public dependency workflow `cargo instrument --with-dependencies -- build` (policy `dependencies-v1`) with ambient `CARGO_INSTRUMENT_*`, `INSTRUMENT_DEBUG`, `RUSTC_WRAPPER`, and fault-injection variables removed; instrumented compile times are public-command wall time including the JSON pre-pass, orchestration, mirroring, and rewriting. The release build asserts and prints the emitter route (`EMITTER:` lines above): native R-4 for `bench_dep`, no wrapper instrumentation for `bench_app`. Runtime measures generated dependency spans with an OpenTelemetry SDK counting processor and no exporter; provider setup and `otel_shim::init()` run before the timed loop. Each instrumented sample asserts 500,000 completed dependency spans inside the application; each baseline asserts zero. Build and runtime pairs alternate baseline-first and instrumented-first order. Measured runtime samples (N=10) follow one discarded warm-up per variant. Raw per-run samples are printed as `RAW sample` lines; only medians feed the tables. This synchronous microbenchmark does not measure async application overhead, and parent-child ancestry of the counted spans is not verified here.

